codex
- [RESOLVED] Finding 1 — loginMode import/reset no longer desynchronizes account state.
  `GStorage.importAllJsonSettings` preserves the current `loginMode`, and About reset restores it after clearing settings. `MineController._onLogoutMain` also avoids deleting accounts after anonymous “未登录” responses.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 2 — required non-deferred account endpoints were added.
  The policy now includes favorite-folder contents, media playlists, account profile load/edit endpoints, and live favorite tag saving. Feed dislike remains omitted, but the finding explicitly marked that part deferred.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 3 — incognito indicator now follows loginMode only.
  `MineController.anonymity` is derived from `!LoginPolicy.loginMode`, and heartbeat-role updates no longer mutate it.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 4 — member relation is fetched separately.
  Member space still loads anonymously, but `_queryRelation()` now fetches the logged-in relation via `UserHttp.userRelation(mid)` when appropriate.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 5 — live socket no longer sends account uid with anonymous token.
  The auth packet now sends `uid: 0`, matching the anonymously fetched danmaku token.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 6 — WebView default cookies are anonymous.
  Startup and `onLoginMain` now call `setAnonymousWebCookie()`, while account cookies are only injected for explicit note/account flows.

- [PARTIAL] Finding 7 — deletion/orphan and overlap fixed, but request volume remains high.
  Extras now run through a serial queue and deletion cancels/awaits the running export, which addresses overlap and orphan recreation. However defaults remain 200 root comments and 10 replies per root in `lib/pages/setting/models/download_settings.dart:40-54`, so the per-video request burst concern remains.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 8 — 416 handling and retry budget are improved.
  A 416 without a usable total now probes size and never truncates non-empty saved bytes just on uncertainty. Retry failures also reset when saved bytes advance.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 9 — merge guards are now per-cid.
  `_mergingCids` and `_mergeDeletedCids` replace the single shared fields, so overlapping merges do not clobber each other.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 10 — Type1 merge now uses index segment count.
  `_mergeDownload` reads `segment_list.length` from `index.json` and deletes higher stale segments.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 11 — scoped fallback issues were addressed.
  Join/remux failures now fall back for general exceptions, sniffed extensions avoid naming unknown content `.mp4`, Android scans all exported parts, and merge failure sets `failMerge`. The deferred in-app multi-part playback issue is outside this fix scope.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 12 — logged-out live users keep the danmaku toggle.
  The input bar no longer returns early for logged-out users; it keeps the toggle and hides send/like-only affordances.

- [PARTIAL] Finding 13 — runtime file forwarding fixed, Linux desktop registration still incomplete.
  `app_scheme.dart` now recognizes plain local paths and `file:` URIs, and avoids double-opening the launch file. But `assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop:6-10` still uses `Exec=librepili %u` and only registers `x-scheme-handler/bilibili`, so video MIME “Open With” integration is still not advertised.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 14 — common XML danmaku forms are supported.
  The loader now checks both `base.danmaku.xml` and `base.xml`, accepts attributes/single quotes, and decodes numeric entities.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 15 — local feed now caches per UP.
  The feed keeps a 30-minute per-UP cache and refetches only stale/missing follows unless the user manually refreshes.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 16 — self-test isolation improved.
  Self-test gets a separate temp subdirectory, and Linux self-test launches set `G_APPLICATION_NON_UNIQUE` before registration.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 17 — local/offline playback no longer heartbeats.
  Heartbeat reporting now returns early for `isFileSource`.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 18 — local favorite folders remain visible on account query failure.
  The error branch now renders the local section before the account error and saves only local choices when account folders failed.

- [PARTIAL] Finding 19 — long Windows export paths were not really addressed.
  The fix reuses stale `.part` folders, but the folder/file naming still repeats the long base name and appends extras suffixes in `lib/services/download/download_service.dart:888-936`. No real probe or path-length mitigation was added.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 20 — LocalLibrary import validates before clearing.
  `LocalLibrary.checkImport` parses all provided local boxes before any box is cleared, preventing malformed backups from wiping follows/favorites.

- [RESOLVED] Finding 21 — removed Windows exe updater option.
  The update dialog now offers only the Windows zip.

TOTAL: ROUND-NEEDS-FIX
